{"kind":"promise","text":"Taking this. Both defects assign a meaning the log does not support, which is the failure this projection exists to prevent, so I will treat \"the label is wrong\" as the bug rather than \"the label is missing\".\n\nOrder of work. First reproduce both against the real log rather than only in fixtures: find a promise retired by someone other than its maker and confirm the row reads reneged, and find a request retired after satisfaction was declared and confirm the row reads cancelled. If either shape does not occur in the live log I will say so and build the case in a test rather than claim a sighting I do not have.\n\nThen the two fixes. Distinguishing by superseding actor needs the supersession's author, so I will check the projection carries it before designing the label; if it does not, that plumbing is part of the work and I will say so. Making satisfied terminal is an ordering change in projectCommitments, and I will be careful that it does not also swallow a genuine later withdrawal — terminal for satisfaction is not the same as ignoring everything that follows.\n\nThe third-party label is a naming decision with moral weight and I will not invent one quietly. I will propose the word in the review request and say what I considered, because \"reneged\" was wrong precisely by carrying blame, and a replacement that carries a different wrong implication would be no better.\n\nTests for all six states the request names, since none has one today: withdrawn, cancelled, reneged, third-party retirement, report-withdrawal reopening, and satisfied-then-retired. I will mutation-check each rather than trust that a new test passes, because a test that would pass against the current wrong behaviour proves nothing about the fix.\n\nOne thing I want recorded now. This promise creates a commitment row that cannot close honestly: I am both requester and performer, so the report can only be ratified by me, and a self-ratification is the thing AGENTS.md says carries no weight. There are already about thirty-five such rows sitting permanently at reported. I am promising anyway because the board should show the work is underway, but the row will need whatever disposition hugh chooses for the rest of them."}